#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.proxy"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:10
msgid ""
"Override the HTTP proxy, normally configured using the 'http_proxy', "
"'https_proxy', and 'all_proxy' environment variables (see `curl(1)`). In "
"addition to the syntax understood by curl, it is possible to specify a proxy "
"string with a user name but no password, in which case git will attempt to "
"acquire one in the same way it does for other credentials. See "
"linkgit:gitcredentials[7] for more information. The syntax thus is "
"'[protocol://][user[:password]@]proxyhost[:port][/path]'. This can be "
"overridden on a per-remote basis; see remote.<name>.proxy"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:15
msgid ""
"Any proxy, however configured, must be completely transparent and must not "
"modify, transform, or buffer the request or response in any way.  Proxies "
"which are not completely transparent are known to cause various forms of "
"breakage with Git."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.proxyAuthMethod"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:23
msgid ""
"Set the method with which to authenticate against the HTTP proxy. This only "
"takes effect if the configured proxy string contains a user name part "
"(i.e. is of the form 'user@host' or 'user@host:port'). This can be "
"overridden on a per-remote basis; see `remote.<name>.proxyAuthMethod`.  Both "
"can be overridden by the `GIT_HTTP_PROXY_AUTHMETHOD` environment variable.  "
"Possible values are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:29
msgid ""
"`anyauth` - Automatically pick a suitable authentication method. It is "
"assumed that the proxy answers an unauthenticated request with a 407 status "
"code and one or more Proxy-authenticate headers with supported "
"authentication methods. This is the default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:30
msgid "`basic` - HTTP Basic authentication"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:32
msgid ""
"`digest` - HTTP Digest authentication; this prevents the password from being "
"transmitted to the proxy in clear text"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:34
msgid ""
"`negotiate` - GSS-Negotiate authentication (compare the --negotiate option "
"of `curl(1)`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:35
msgid "`ntlm` - NTLM authentication (compare the --ntlm option of `curl(1)`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.proxySSLCert"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:41
msgid ""
"The pathname of a file that stores a client certificate to use to "
"authenticate with an HTTPS proxy. Can be overridden by the "
"`GIT_PROXY_SSL_CERT` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.proxySSLKey"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:46
msgid ""
"The pathname of a file that stores a private key to use to authenticate with "
"an HTTPS proxy. Can be overridden by the `GIT_PROXY_SSL_KEY` environment "
"variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.proxySSLCertPasswordProtected"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:52
msgid ""
"Enable Git's password prompt for the proxy SSL certificate.  Otherwise "
"OpenSSL will prompt the user, possibly many times, if the certificate or "
"private key is encrypted. Can be overridden by the "
"`GIT_PROXY_SSL_CERT_PASSWORD_PROTECTED` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.proxySSLCAInfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:57
msgid ""
"Pathname to the file containing the certificate bundle that should be used "
"to verify the proxy with when using an HTTPS proxy. Can be overridden by the "
"`GIT_PROXY_SSL_CAINFO` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.emptyAuth"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:63
msgid ""
"Attempt authentication without seeking a username or password.  This can be "
"used to attempt GSS-Negotiate authentication without specifying a username "
"in the URL, as libcurl normally requires a username for authentication."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.proactiveAuth"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:68
msgid ""
"Attempt authentication without first making an unauthenticated attempt and "
"receiving a 401 response. This can be used to ensure that all requests are "
"authenticated. If `http.emptyAuth` is set to true, this value has no effect."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:73
msgid ""
"If the credential helper used specifies an authentication scheme (i.e., via "
"the `authtype` field), that value will be used; if a username and password "
"is provided without a scheme, then Basic authentication is used.  The value "
"of the option determines the scheme requested from the helper. Possible "
"values are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:76
msgid "`basic` - Request Basic authentication from the helper."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:77
msgid "`auto` - Allow the helper to pick an appropriate scheme."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:78
msgid "`none` - Disable proactive authentication."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:83
msgid ""
"Note that TLS should always be used with this configuration, since otherwise "
"it is easy to accidentally expose plaintext credentials if Basic "
"authentication is selected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:84
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.delegation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:89
msgid ""
"Control GSSAPI credential delegation. The delegation is disabled by default "
"in libcurl since version 7.21.7. Set parameter to tell the server what it is "
"allowed to delegate when it comes to user credentials. Used with "
"GSS/kerberos. Possible values are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:92
msgid "`none` - Don't allow any delegation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:94
msgid ""
"`policy` - Delegates if and only if the OK-AS-DELEGATE flag is set in the "
"Kerberos service ticket, which is a matter of realm policy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:95
msgid "`always` - Unconditionally allow the server to delegate."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:98
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.extraHeader"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:103
msgid ""
"Pass an additional HTTP header when communicating with a server.  If more "
"than one such entry exists, all of them are added as extra headers.  To "
"allow overriding the settings inherited from the system config, an empty "
"value will reset the extra headers to the empty list."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:104
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.cookieFile"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:115
msgid ""
"The pathname of a file containing previously stored cookie lines, which "
"should be used in the Git http session, if they match the server. The file "
"format of the file to read cookies from should be plain HTTP headers or the "
"Netscape/Mozilla cookie file format (see `curl(1)`).  Set it to an empty "
"string, to accept only new cookies from the server and send them back in "
"successive requests within same connection.  NOTE that the file specified "
"with http.cookieFile is used only as input unless http.saveCookies is set."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.saveCookies"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:120
msgid ""
"If set, store cookies received during requests to the file specified by "
"http.cookieFile. Has no effect if http.cookieFile is unset, or set to an "
"empty string."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:121
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.version"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:126
msgid ""
"Use the specified HTTP protocol version when communicating with a server.  "
"If you want to force the default. The available and default version depend "
"on libcurl. Currently the possible values of this option are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:128
msgid "HTTP/2"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:129
msgid "HTTP/1.1"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:130
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.curloptResolve"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:134
msgid ""
"Hostname resolution information that will be used first by libcurl when "
"sending HTTP requests.  This information should be in one of the following "
"formats:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:136
msgid "[+]HOST:PORT:ADDRESS[,ADDRESS]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:137
msgid "-HOST:PORT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:145
msgid ""
"The first format redirects all requests to the given `HOST:PORT` to the "
"provided `ADDRESS`(s). The second format clears all previous config values "
"for that `HOST:PORT` combination.  To allow easy overriding of all the "
"settings inherited from the system config, an empty value will reset all "
"resolution information to the empty list."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:146
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.sslVersion"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:155
msgid ""
"The SSL version to use when negotiating an SSL connection, if you want to "
"force the default.  The available and default version depend on whether "
"libcurl was built against NSS or OpenSSL and the particular configuration of "
"the crypto library in use. Internally this sets the 'CURLOPT_SSL_VERSION' "
"option; see the libcurl documentation for more details on the format of this "
"option and for the ssl version supported. Currently the possible values of "
"this option are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:157
msgid "sslv2"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:158
msgid "sslv3"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:159
msgid "tlsv1"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:160
msgid "tlsv1.0"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:161
msgid "tlsv1.1"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:162
msgid "tlsv1.2"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:163
msgid "tlsv1.3"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:169
msgid ""
"Can be overridden by the `GIT_SSL_VERSION` environment variable.  To force "
"git to use libcurl's default ssl version and ignore any explicit "
"http.sslversion option, set `GIT_SSL_VERSION` to the empty string."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:170
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.sslCipherList"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:177
msgid ""
"A list of SSL ciphers to use when negotiating an SSL connection.  The "
"available ciphers depend on whether libcurl was built against NSS or OpenSSL "
"and the particular configuration of the crypto library in use.  Internally "
"this sets the 'CURLOPT_SSL_CIPHER_LIST' option; see the libcurl "
"documentation for more details on the format of this list."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:182
msgid ""
"Can be overridden by the `GIT_SSL_CIPHER_LIST` environment variable.  To "
"force git to use libcurl's default cipher list and ignore any explicit "
"http.sslCipherList option, set `GIT_SSL_CIPHER_LIST` to the empty string."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:183
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.sslVerify"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:187
msgid ""
"Whether to verify the SSL certificate when fetching or pushing over "
"HTTPS. Defaults to true. Can be overridden by the `GIT_SSL_NO_VERIFY` "
"environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:188
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.sslCert"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:192
msgid ""
"File containing the SSL certificate when fetching or pushing over HTTPS. Can "
"be overridden by the `GIT_SSL_CERT` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:193
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.sslKey"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:197
msgid ""
"File containing the SSL private key when fetching or pushing over HTTPS. Can "
"be overridden by the `GIT_SSL_KEY` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:198
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.sslCertPasswordProtected"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:203
msgid ""
"Enable Git's password prompt for the SSL certificate.  Otherwise OpenSSL "
"will prompt the user, possibly many times, if the certificate or private key "
"is encrypted.  Can be overridden by the `GIT_SSL_CERT_PASSWORD_PROTECTED` "
"environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:204
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.sslCAInfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:208
msgid ""
"File containing the certificates to verify the peer with when fetching or "
"pushing over HTTPS. Can be overridden by the `GIT_SSL_CAINFO` environment "
"variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:209
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.sslCAPath"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:213
msgid ""
"Path containing files with the CA certificates to verify the peer with when "
"fetching or pushing over HTTPS. Can be overridden by the `GIT_SSL_CAPATH` "
"environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:214
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.sslBackend"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:218
msgid ""
"Name of the SSL backend to use (e.g. \"openssl\" or \"schannel\").  This "
"option is ignored if cURL lacks support for choosing the SSL backend at "
"runtime."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:219
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.sslCertType"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:225
msgid ""
"Type of client certificate used when fetching or pushing over HTTPS.  "
"\"PEM\", \"DER\" are supported when using openssl or gnutls "
"backends. \"P12\" is supported on \"openssl\", \"schannel\", "
"\"securetransport\", and gnutls 8.11+.  See also libcurl "
"`CURLOPT_SSLCERTTYPE`. Can be overridden by the `GIT_SSL_CERT_TYPE` "
"environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:226
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.sslKeyType"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:233
msgid ""
"Type of client private key used when fetching or pushing over HTTPS. (e.g.  "
"\"PEM\", \"DER\", or \"ENG\"). Only applicable when using \"openssl\" "
"backend. \"DER\" is not supported with openssl. Particularly useful when set "
"to \"ENG\" for authenticating with PKCS#11 tokens, with a PKCS#11 URL in "
"sslCert option.  See also libcurl `CURLOPT_SSLKEYTYPE`. Can be overridden by "
"the `GIT_SSL_KEY_TYPE` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:234
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.schannelCheckRevoke"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:241
msgid ""
"Used to enforce or disable certificate revocation checks in cURL when "
"http.sslBackend is set to \"schannel\". Defaults to `true` if unset. Only "
"necessary to disable this if Git consistently errors and the message is "
"about checking the revocation status of a certificate. This option is "
"ignored if cURL lacks support for setting the relevant SSL option at "
"runtime."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:242
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.schannelUseSSLCAInfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:249
msgid ""
"As of cURL v7.60.0, the Secure Channel backend can use the certificate "
"bundle provided via `http.sslCAInfo`, but that would override the Windows "
"Certificate Store. Since this is not desirable by default, Git will tell "
"cURL not to use that bundle by default when the `schannel` backend was "
"configured via `http.sslBackend`, unless `http.schannelUseSSLCAInfo` "
"overrides this behavior."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:250
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.pinnedPubkey"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:257
msgid ""
"Public key of the https service. It may either be the filename of a PEM or "
"DER encoded public key file or a string starting with 'sha256//' followed by "
"the base64 encoded sha256 hash of the public key. See also libcurl "
"'CURLOPT_PINNEDPUBLICKEY'. git will exit with an error if this option is set "
"but not supported by cURL."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:258
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.sslTry"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:265
msgid ""
"Attempt to use AUTH SSL/TLS and encrypted data transfers when connecting via "
"regular FTP protocol. This might be needed if the FTP server requires it for "
"security reasons or you wish to connect securely whenever remote FTP server "
"supports it.  Default is false since it might trigger certificate "
"verification errors on misconfigured servers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:266
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.maxRequests"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:269
msgid ""
"How many HTTP requests to launch in parallel. Can be overridden by the "
"`GIT_HTTP_MAX_REQUESTS` environment variable. Default is 5."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:270
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.minSessions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:275
msgid ""
"The number of curl sessions (counted across slots) to be kept across "
"requests. They will not be ended with curl_easy_cleanup() until "
"http_cleanup() is invoked. If USE_CURL_MULTI is not defined, this value will "
"be capped at 1. Defaults to 1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:276
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.postBuffer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:283
msgid ""
"Maximum size in bytes of the buffer used by smart HTTP transports when "
"POSTing data to the remote system.  For requests larger than this buffer "
"size, HTTP/1.1 and Transfer-Encoding: chunked is used to avoid creating a "
"massive pack file locally.  Default is 1 MiB, which is sufficient for most "
"requests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:291
msgid ""
"Note that raising this limit is only effective for disabling chunked "
"transfer encoding and therefore should be used only where the remote server "
"or a proxy only supports HTTP/1.0 or is noncompliant with the HTTP "
"standard.  Raising this is not, in general, an effective solution for most "
"push problems, but can increase memory consumption significantly since the "
"entire buffer is allocated even for small pushes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:292
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.lowSpeedLimit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:293
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.lowSpeedTime"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:299
msgid ""
"If the HTTP transfer speed, in bytes per second, is less than "
"'http.lowSpeedLimit' for longer than 'http.lowSpeedTime' seconds, the "
"transfer is aborted.  Can be overridden by the `GIT_HTTP_LOW_SPEED_LIMIT` "
"and `GIT_HTTP_LOW_SPEED_TIME` environment variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:300
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.keepAliveIdle"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:305
msgid ""
"Specifies how long in seconds to wait on an idle connection before sending "
"TCP keepalive probes (if supported by the OS). If unset, curl's default "
"value is used. Can be overridden by the `GIT_HTTP_KEEPALIVE_IDLE` "
"environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:306
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.keepAliveInterval"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:311
msgid ""
"Specifies how long in seconds to wait between TCP keepalive probes (if "
"supported by the OS). If unset, curl's default value is used. Can be "
"overridden by the `GIT_HTTP_KEEPALIVE_INTERVAL` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:312
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.keepAliveCount"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:317
msgid ""
"Specifies how many TCP keepalive probes to send before giving up and "
"terminating the connection (if supported by the OS). If unset, curl's "
"default value is used. Can be overridden by the `GIT_HTTP_KEEPALIVE_COUNT` "
"environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:318
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.noEPSV"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:323
msgid ""
"A boolean which disables using of EPSV ftp command by curl.  This can be "
"helpful with some \"poor\" ftp servers which don't support EPSV mode. Can be "
"overridden by the `GIT_CURL_FTP_NO_EPSV` environment variable. Default is "
"false (curl will use EPSV)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:324
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.userAgent"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:332
msgid ""
"The HTTP USER_AGENT string presented to an HTTP server.  The default value "
"represents the version of the Git client such as git/1.7.1.  This option "
"allows you to override this value to a more common value such as "
"Mozilla/4.0.  This may be necessary, for instance, if connecting through a "
"firewall that restricts HTTP connections to a set of common USER_AGENT "
"strings (but not including those like git/1.7.1).  Can be overridden by the "
"`GIT_HTTP_USER_AGENT` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:333
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.followRedirects"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:342
msgid ""
"Whether git should follow HTTP redirects. If set to `true`, git will "
"transparently follow any redirect issued by a server it encounters. If set "
"to `false`, git will treat all redirects as errors. If set to `initial`, git "
"will follow redirects only for the initial request to a remote, but not for "
"subsequent follow-up HTTP requests. Since git uses the redirected URL as the "
"base for the follow-up requests, this is generally sufficient. The default "
"is `initial`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:343
#, no-wrap
msgid "http.<url>.*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:347
msgid ""
"Any of the http.* options above can be applied selectively to some URLs.  "
"For a config key to match a URL, each element of the config key is compared "
"to that of the URL, in the following order:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:351
msgid ""
"Scheme (e.g., `https` in `https://example.com/`). This field must match "
"exactly between the config key and the URL."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:357
msgid ""
"Host/domain name (e.g., `example.com` in `https://example.com/`).  This "
"field must match between the config key and the URL. It is possible to "
"specify a `*` as part of the host name to match all subdomains at this "
"level. `https://*.example.com/` for example would match "
"`https://foo.example.com/`, but not `https://foo.bar.example.com/`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:362
msgid ""
"Port number (e.g., `8080` in `http://example.com:8080/`).  This field must "
"match exactly between the config key and the URL.  Omitted port numbers are "
"automatically converted to the correct default for the scheme before "
"matching."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:370
msgid ""
"Path (e.g., `repo.git` in `https://example.com/repo.git`). The path field of "
"the config key must match the path field of the URL either exactly or as a "
"prefix of slash-delimited path elements.  This means a config key with path "
"`foo/` matches URL path `foo/bar`.  A prefix can only match on a slash (`/`) "
"boundary.  Longer matches take precedence (so a config key with path "
"`foo/bar` is a better match to URL path `foo/bar` than a config key with "
"just path `foo/`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:376
msgid ""
"User name (e.g., `user` in `https://user@example.com/repo.git`). If the "
"config key has a user name it must match the user name in the URL "
"exactly. If the config key does not have a user name, that config key will "
"match a URL with any user name (including none), but at a lower precedence "
"than a config key with a user name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:383
msgid ""
"The list above is ordered by decreasing precedence; a URL that matches a "
"config key's path is preferred to one that matches its user name. For "
"example, if the URL is `https://user@example.com/foo/bar` a config key match "
"of `https://example.com/foo` will be preferred over a config key match of "
"`https://user@example.com`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/http.adoc:389
msgid ""
"All URLs are normalized before attempting any matching (the password part, "
"if embedded in the URL, is always ignored for matching purposes) so that "
"equivalent URLs that are simply spelled differently will match properly.  "
"Environment variable settings always override any matches.  The URLs that "
"are matched against are those given directly to Git commands.  This means "
"any URLs visited as a result of a redirection do not participate in "
"matching."
msgstr ""
